amend(242,items=['SA07-241'],his_statement='this cannot work as Serre pointed out',
      statement='The proposed route is: arbitrary X birational to a smooth X′, which is a specialization of a smooth X″ itself birational to a smooth hypersurface. The letter withdraws this route because it would force X to be simply connected in the relevant dimension. It then asks for a reformulation using singular hypersurfaces. This is a failure of the proposed geometric reduction, not merely a withdrawal of novelty.',
      **{'class':'D'},
      present_status='As of 2026-11-19: The proposed route is explicitly withdrawn. The precise birational/specialization steps are retained; no stronger universal non-domination statement is inferred.')
