amend(251,statement='The EGA editorial note retains the inseparable residue-field obstruction at the closed point of a complete local k-algebra finite over a power-series ring, and requests removal of a second draft paragraph. That visible paragraph forms J=ker(A→A_p), sets A′=A/J, identifies A_p≅A′_p′, and tries to remove a minimal-prime dimension hypothesis by lifting a finite map B→A′ to B→A; its final conclusion is cut off.',
      fate='Published EGAIV4 Remark18.11.6, p.176, reproduces the first obstruction paragraph; the second draft paragraph is absent. The complete primary PDF was downloaded and the exact Remark read after the web tool rejected its49.85MB size. The local quotient identities in the visible draft are valid; finiteness of an arbitrary lift B→A does not follow solely from finiteness B→A′, so the cut-off conclusion must not be supplied.',
      present_status='As of 2026-11-19: Exact first-paragraph published counterpart verified. The visible cancelled second argument and its missing final clause are recorded separately, rather than called wholly unavailable.',confidence='high')
amend(264,fate='Karoubi’s own bibliography lists Cohomologie des catégories de Banach, CRAS263(1966), pp.275–278,341–344,357–360. The first note PDFp1/printed275 was visually opened: its introduction and Definition1.1 are the exact counterpart of the reused leaf, continuing with continuity, direct sums and kernels of idempotents. His1968 Annales ENS paper is a bibliographically verified later development; no unseen theorem in it is used as proof.',
      fate_date='First note dated22August1966; full paper1968')
amend(265,his_statement='Φ_L(F)=R pr_(2*) (L pr_1^*(F)⊗L)',
      statement='For an abelian scheme A/S over an arbitrary scheme S, an S-scheme X and a rigidified fibrewise algebraically trivial line bundle L on A×_S X, the kernel construction sends perfect complexes on A to perfect complexes on X. It is the base change of the normalized Poincaré transform along the classifying map X→A^∨. The coherent bounded version additionally uses the noetherian hypotheses of the cited relative exposition.',
      fate='Stacks0DJT Lemma36.35.10 and0FYP Lemma57.8.4(3) give perfect direct image and arbitrary derived base change under proper flat finite presentation, exactly applicable to A×_S X→X. Laumon1996 §§1.1–1.2 gives the dual abelian-scheme and bounded coherent formulation. These support the manuscript’s arbitrary-base perfect-complex proposition without changing parf|prof on the ink.',
      refs=['Stacks0DJT','Stacks0FYP','Laumon1996','Beauville1983'])
amend(266,statement='For the rigidified fibrewise algebraically trivial kernel of CL-SA07-265, the Poincaré biextension identity and derived base change give Φ_L(F*_A G)≅Φ_L(F)⊗^LΦ_L(G) for perfect F,G. The assertion applies to every parameter scheme X via X→A^∨, not only to the dual itself. Over a field the rational Chow forward formula has no parity sign.',refs=['Laumon1996','Beauville1983','Kleiman1968','Stacks0DJT'])
amend(267,his_statement='quelconques faisceaux L,L′,L″',
      statement='The margin extends the binary convolution-to-tensor identity to a flat group with the explicitly written multiplicative kernel, then to a map π:P×_S Q→R and three kernels satisfying (π×id)^*L≅pr_13^*L′⊗^Lpr_23^*L″. With quasi-compact/quasi-separated schemes, derived base change, projection formula and suitable proper-support/Tor conditions, the same binary identity follows. It asserts no Fourier equivalence or dual object for every flat group.',
      status_on_pages='generalization sketched in the margin; categorical domain and associativity/unit coherence not completed',
      computation='computations.md §10 gives the three-kernel binary calculation and states sufficient derived-operation hypotheses',
      **{'class':'B'},
      fate='Stacks0FYP Lemmas57.8.2–57.8.5 give the exact modern kernel calculus, Tor-independent composition and proper-support preservation statements. The binary formula follows by the same projection/base-change calculation. The earlier-run proposal of a monoidal functor additionally needs coherent unit/associativity data; that is a proposal, not a missing duality theorem in the manuscript.',
      present_status='As of 2026-11-19: The binary kernel identity is established under explicit derived-operation hypotheses. A monoidal enhancement requires coherence data and no general Fourier equivalence is asserted.',refs=['Stacks0FYP','Stacks0DJT','Laumon1996'],confidence='high')
amend(275,statement='For relative perfect K-classes on an abelian scheme, virtual rank and fibrewise Euler characteristic are locally constant functions on S and satisfy ε_BΦ=χ_A and χ_BΦ=(−1)^gε_A. On a field these are the usual integer equalities. The line τ has rank1 and the shift accounts for the parity.',
      fate='Laumon1996 inversion and base-change formulas establish the equalities; Stacks0DJT supplies the relative perfect direct image. The manuscript explicitly locates them in H⁰(S,Z), so restricting its statement to fields would understate it.',refs=['Laumon1996','Beauville1983','Stacks0DJT'])
amend(276,fate='Beauville1983 Proposition5, pp.248–249, treats the symmetric ample field case and the dual-polarization exponential. The manuscript allows relative Picard components; Laumon1996 fixes the derived determinant convention. The relative component formula is recorded with the signed δ′ convention, while the explicit Chern computation below is verified only in the specified ample field case.',confidence='medium')
amend(277,statement='In the verified ample field case, let L be ample on an abelian variety over an algebraically closed field, r=χ(L)>0 and E=Φ_P(L). The isogeny pullback φ_L^*E≅H⁰(L)⊗L^−1 gives ch(E)=r exp(−D′/r), with D′=−c₁(E). Hence c_t(E)=(1−D′t/r)^r and c_k=(−1)^k[(r−1)…(r−k+1)/(k!r^(k−1))]D′^k. The general relative heuristic is not asserted proved by this case.',
      fate='Beauville1983 Proposition5 supplies the ample symmetric Fourier formula; the Poincaré translation/isogeny calculation gives the ample bundle formula, which is re-derived in computations.md. The exact Mukai Proposition3.11 source is followed via the opened Stacks bibliography rather than cited from memory. No actual fractional line bundle is produced.',
      present_status='As of 2026-11-19: Established in the explicit ample field case and as a formal consequence whenever the character identity holds. Arbitrary-base strengthening remains separately qualified.')
amend(281,his_statement='ces formules sont-elles bien vraies mod torsion?',
      statement='The literal question concerns the preceding formal-power, Chern-character and Chern-class formulas for a particular transformed line bundle, in the manuscript K/Gr context. In the ample field case the corrected formulas hold in rational Chow theory; clearing denominators gives integral equalities modulo torsion. They neither define a fractional line bundle nor assert that Fourier preserves the whole integral Chow group. Relative-base/filtration and torsion-sensitive meanings remain unspecified.',
      computation='C07 and computations.md §10 establish the corrected particular-bundle formulas and distinguish rational equality, cleared-denominator equality modulo torsion, and an integral transform on all cycles.',
      fate='The particular-bundle rational formula is established by the ample isogeny calculation (Beauville1983 Proposition5). As a separate stronger comparison, Beckmann–de Gaay Fortman2023 Theorem3.8 characterizes integral Fourier on entire Chow groups. Engel–de Gaay Fortman–Schreieder2025/2026 Theorem1.1 gives very general complex PPAV counterexamples to that stronger assertion, and Kahn2026 Theorem1.2/Corollary1.3 supplies an étale-Chow replacement after its characteristic/2-torsion qualifications. Those are not counterexamples or solutions to every possible interpretation of the leaf’s narrower question.',
      present_status='As of 2026-11-19: Corrected ample-field formulas are known rationally and after clearing denominators modulo torsion. The unspecified relative K/Gr assertion needs formulation. The stronger entire-Chow integral extrapolation is false, but is not attributed to Grothendieck here.',
      refs=['Beauville1983','BeckmannFortman2023','EngelFortmanSchreieder2025','Kahn2026'])

