amend(298,fate='Grothendieck1969 pp.194–197 and Kleiman1968 §§3.2–3.3 formulate primitive Hodge-type positivity. ACMV2025 Theorem12.6, pp.66–67, constructs a symmetric morphism/isogeny with explicit Bloch-map and Tate-module hypotheses. Theorem12.12(3), p.68, gives a distinguished symmetric isomorphism for a smooth projective threefold over a perfect field with universally trivial CH0; over a subfield of C its negative agrees with the principal Hodge polarization. Chapter13, p.71 onward, requires lifting/specialization hypotheses to prove polarization in positive characteristic. These exact statements were opened; no all-codimension unconditional positivity theorem is inferred.')
